      "evidence": "The software provides pricing/scheduling tools that the licensed contractor (the professional of record) reviews and sends as their own quote. It does not hold customer funds, does not act as the licensed contractor, and does not give regulated professional advice (legal/medical/investment). Contractor licensing itself is a customer-side requirement, not the software vendor's.",
